## Tighten input validation site-wide

### Status
In progress — working section by section (see Implementation Plan below). Sections 1-3 landed;
next up is Section 4.

### Implementation Plan
Broken into sections so work can span multiple sessions. Check off as each section lands.
- [x] **Section 1 — Bug fixes: rebind to view models.** Rebound `UpdateDetails`/`AddFinalDate` to
      new `EventUpdateDetailsViewModel`/`EventAddFinalDateViewModel`; added `asp-validation-for`/
      summary markup + `_ValidationScriptsPartial` to `Settings.cshtml`/`Finalize.cshtml`/
      `_FinalizeCallTheDateCard.cshtml`. Folded in the emoji single-grapheme-cluster check (new
      `SingleGraphemeAttribute` in `Common/`, with a matching client-side jQuery Validate rule in
      `site.js`) and final-date bounds (±50yr via shared `ModelConstants.UserSuppliedDateBoundYears`,
      reused by `EventsController.Availability.cs`'s existing bound too; 40-row cap via
      `ModelConstants.EventFinalDateMaxCount`; malformed dates now render a friendly `ModelState`
      error instead of a bare 400). Added/updated tests in
      `EventsControllerSettingsTests`/`EventsControllerFinalDateTests`/new
      `EventUpdateDetailsViewModelTests`/`EventAddFinalDateViewModelTests`/
      `SingleGraphemeAttributeTests`.
- [x] **Section 2 — Site-wide consistency.** Added `_ValidationScriptsPartial` to
      `Views/Home/Index.cshtml`. Applied `ModelConstants.DisplayNameContentPattern` to
      `EventSignInViewModel.DisplayName`, `Participant.DisplayName`, `Event.Title`,
      `IndexViewModel.CreateEventName`, and `EventUpdateDetailsViewModel.Title` (the last one is
      the actual POST-bound target for title edits, so it needed the pattern directly rather than
      relying on the `Event` entity's copy). Added a new `ModelConstants.DescriptionContentPattern`
      (same control-character/zero-width rejection as `DisplayNameContentPattern`, written with
      `[\s\S]` instead of `.` so it still scans past embedded newlines, and permitting `\n`/`\r`
      themselves) applied to `EventSettings.Description` and `EventUpdateDetailsViewModel.Description`.
      Trimming for all of the above was already in place from Section 1's rebind
      (`UpdateDetails`/`Create`/`Join`/`SignIn` all trim before validating). Audited
      Models/Controllers/Views for ad-hoc length literals — found none; every `[StringLength]`/
      `maxlength` already sources from `ModelConstants`. Added matching test coverage: control-
      character/zero-width/non-Latin/whitespace-only edge cases for every property that gained
      `DisplayNameContentPattern` (`IndexViewModelTests`, `EventSignInViewModelTests`,
      `ParticipantTests`, `EventTests`, `EventUpdateDetailsViewModelTests`), the same plus
      multiline-specific cases (embedded `\n`/`\r` accepted, a bad character *after* an embedded
      newline still rejected, embedded raw tab still rejected) for `DescriptionContentPattern`
      (`EventUpdateDetailsViewModelTests`, new `EventSettingsTests`), and `DescriptionContentPattern`
      added to `ModelConstantsTests`' pattern-coherence checks.
- [x] **Section 3 — NFC normalization.** Added `Services/TextNormalizer.NormalizeToNfc`, a small
      static helper (`UniqueCodeGenerator`/`ColorContrastHelper`-style utility, no DI dependency
      needed) that normalizes to Unicode Normalization Form C, returning null/empty input
      unchanged. Audited every identity-bearing free-text field site-wide for a uniqueness/equality
      check it could defeat via codepoint-composition differences — the only one found was
      `Participant.DisplayName` via `EventsController.SignIn.cs`'s `ValidateParticipantUniquenessAsync`
      (`Event.Title`/descriptions have no such check, and `ApplicationUser`'s email uniqueness goes
      through Identity's own normalized-email column, untouched here). Applied
      `TextNormalizer.NormalizeToNfc` in `NormalizeSignInModel` to both `DisplayName` and
      `SelectedExistingDisplayName` (the latter so a decomposed-form dropdown selection still
      resolves to its composed, already-normalized stored counterpart in
      `GetSelectedExistingParticipantAsync`). Also adopted the same helper on `ApplicationUser.DisplayName`
      in `Register.cshtml.cs`, `ExternalLogin.cshtml.cs`, and `Manage/Index.cshtml.cs` for
      consistency, even though no uniqueness check currently reads that field — `Manage/Index.cshtml.cs`
      normalizes before its dirty-check comparison so an already-normalized name round-tripping
      through the form doesn't trigger a spurious `UpdateAsync`. Added
      `WhenWorksWeb.Tests/Services/TextNormalizerTests.cs` (null/empty/ASCII/idempotency/already-NFC
      short-circuit/non-Latin script coverage, using explicit `\u`-escaped codepoints rather than
      literal accented characters in source so the exact composition under test doesn't depend on
      file encoding) and new `EventsControllerSignInTests` cases: a decomposed submission persists
      NFC-normalized, a decomposed submission matching an existing composed name is still rejected
      as a duplicate, and a decomposed dropdown selection still resolves and updates the existing
      composed participant.
- [ ] **Section 4 — Admin area.** Validation attributes on `ManageUsersModel.Email` +
      corresponding view markup.

### GitHub Issue
#88

### Summary
Extend the validation standard established for the account settings pages (#81/#87) to the rest
of the site: Home (create/join), Events (sign-in, settings, finalize, organizers), MyEvents, and
the Admin area. Also fixes two bugs found while auditing — validation errors that are currently
silently swallowed on two forms.

### Motivation
An audit of every non-Identity form turned up real gaps: two forms where `ModelState` errors can
never reach the user, several fields missing the control-character/zero-width-character rejection
and trimming that Identity pages already got, an event emoji field that accepts arbitrary text,
final dates with no bound on range or count, and an Admin email field with no validation at all.

---

### Proposed Changes

#### Bug fixes — validation errors currently invisible to the user
- `EventsController.Settings.cs`'s `UpdateDetails` takes loose `[FromForm] string title, string?
  description, string? emoji` params and hand-rolls checks with `ModelState.AddModelError(nameof(title), ...)`
  — but `Views/Events/Settings.cshtml` has no `asp-validation-for` spans or validation summary at
  all on the "Shape the plan" form, so every error is silently swallowed.
- `EventsController.FinalDate.cs`'s `AddFinalDate` takes loose `[FromForm] string startDate, string?
  endDate` and has the same problem: the end-before-start `ModelState` error has nowhere to render
  in `Views/Events/Finalize.cshtml` / `_FinalizeFinalDatesCard.cshtml`.
- Fix: rebind both actions to proper view models — `EventUpdateDetailsViewModel` (Title,
  Description, Emoji) and `EventAddFinalDateViewModel` (StartDate, EndDate) — with DataAnnotations,
  matching the `IndexViewModel`/`EventSignInViewModel` pattern used elsewhere. This also fixes the
  ModelState-key mismatch (`nameof(title)` vs. a bound property name) and gets unobtrusive
  client-side validation for free. Add the corresponding `asp-validation-for`/summary markup to
  both views.

#### Consistency with the account-settings standard
- `Views/Home/Index.cshtml` has validation spans but never renders `_ValidationScriptsPartial`
  (unlike `Events/SignIn.cshtml`) — add it so Create/Join get live client-side feedback.
- Apply `ModelConstants.DisplayNameContentPattern` (rejects C0/C1 control chars and zero-width/
  invisible Unicode characters) to `EventSignInViewModel.DisplayName`, `Participant.DisplayName`,
  `Event.Title`, and `IndexViewModel.CreateEventName`.
- Add a new `ModelConstants` pattern for multi-line text — same control-character/zero-width
  rejection as `DisplayNameContentPattern`, but permits `\n`/`\r` — and apply it to
  `EventSettings.Description`.
- Trim all of the above before persisting, matching the account-settings pages' approach.
- Normalize `Participant.DisplayName` (and any other identity-bearing free-text field) to Unicode
  NFC before persisting, so codepoint-composition differences can't defeat
  `EventsController.SignIn.cs`'s `ValidateParticipantUniquenessAsync` per-event uniqueness check.
- Audit every site-wide text field for an explicit max length sourced from `ModelConstants` (no
  ad-hoc magic numbers) and `[Required]`/a minimum length where the field shouldn't be empty.
- Re-check the Identity pages: if this pass introduces a reusable pattern constant or an
  NFC-normalization helper, confirm whether any Identity field should adopt it too.

#### Event emoji field (`EventSettings.Emoji`)
- Replace the current bare `[StringLength(ModelConstants.EventEmojiMaxLength)]` with a check that
  the value is exactly one extended grapheme cluster (via `System.Globalization.StringInfo`) and
  free of control/zero-width characters.
- Deliberately not a "real emoji" codepoint allowlist: .NET regex has no
  `\p{Extended_Pictographic}`-equivalent derived-property support, so an allowlist would mean
  hand-maintaining codepoint ranges that go stale as Unicode adds new emoji each year. The
  grapheme-cluster check closes the actual gap (no arbitrary multi-character text as the icon)
  without that maintenance burden — it doesn't recognize *which* character was picked, only that
  it's a single visible glyph. The field is only ever populated by the `emoji-picker-element`
  web component's `emoji-click` handler, so this is a defense-in-depth check against a
  bypassed/tampered request, not a constraint normal users will hit.

#### Final-date bounds (`EventsController.FinalDate.cs`'s `AddFinalDate`)
- Add a ±50-year date-range bound, extracted into a shared constant/helper reused by
  `EventsController.Availability.cs`'s existing `ToggleAvailabilityDateBoundYears` (currently
  duplicated intent, not duplicated code, between the two files).
- Cap the number of `EventFinalDate` rows per event at 40.
- Make the malformed-date error path consistent: a bare `BadRequest()` today for an unparseable
  `startDate`/`endDate`, vs. a friendly `ModelState` error for end-before-start — both should
  behave the same way once the action is rebound to `EventAddFinalDateViewModel` above.

#### Admin area (`Areas/Admin/Pages/Users/ManageUsers.cshtml(.cs)`)
- Add `[Required]`, `[EmailAddress]`, and `[StringLength(ModelConstants.UserIdMaxLength)]` (or an
  appropriate email-length bound) to `ManageUsersModel.Email`, currently unvalidated beyond a
  manual `IsNullOrWhiteSpace` check in the page handlers.
- Add matching `asp-validation-for`/summary markup to the view.

---

### Acceptance Criteria
- Posting an invalid title/description/emoji to `EventUpdateDetails`, or an invalid final-date
  range to `EventAddFinalDate`, shows a visible, field-specific error instead of silently
  re-rendering the form unchanged.
- Home's Create/Join forms get live client-side validation feedback before submit.
- Event title, participant display name, and event description all reject control characters and
  zero-width/invisible Unicode characters, and reject empty-after-trim values where required.
- A participant/event whose display name differs from an existing one only by Unicode
  normalization form is treated as a duplicate by the uniqueness check.
- The event emoji field rejects any value that isn't a single extended grapheme cluster free of
  control/zero-width characters, both client- and server-side.
- `AddFinalDate` rejects a date more than 50 years from today, rejects an event's 41st final-date
  entry, and returns a friendly, view-rendered error for a malformed date instead of a bare 400.
- The Admin "add admin" form rejects an empty or non-email-shaped value with a visible message.
- Every text field touched by this pass sources its max length from `ModelConstants` rather than
  an inline literal.

### Out of Scope
- Rate limiting/throttling on event or participant creation — a DoS-shaped infrastructure concern
  (middleware, counters, thresholds) separate from field-level validation; would need its own spec.
- Collapsing internal whitespace in display names (e.g. `"Bob    Smith"` vs. `"Bob Smith"`) — raised
  during scoping as a nice-to-have but not confirmed as required.
- `EventDate` availability voting and the `EventMessage` chat system — neither has a controller or
  UI built yet, so their input validation is future feature work, not a retrofit here.
- The hardcoded root-admin address (`kenny@mail.com`) appearing in three places in
  `ManageUsers.cshtml.cs` — unrelated to input validation.
